(see ARCHITECTURE.md for the current writeup + open questions,
ARCHIVE.md for past decisions)

ARCHITECTURE -- STEP BY STEP (option A: client-side fetch + merge)

0. quick fixes before building the merge
   - toolbar click handler checks e.target.closest('#tool-btn'), should
     be '.tool-btn' (buttons are classes now, not ids) -- also currently
     a syntax error (missing closing paren), breaks the whole file
   - images/headshots/siena is missing its extension (should be
     siena.jpg) in both index.html and other.html's <img>
   - cli.js: David confirmed the file split is intentional. No full
     rewrite needed -- just swap the replaceLeft()/replaceRight() calls
     for real links to the new pages, and drop the favorites branch
     (favorites isn't part of the new nav). Since content-only pages
     don't have the cli markup until after the merge (step 1), cli.js
     needs to be loaded dynamically after the merge finishes rather
     than as a static <script> tag on those pages specifically --
     index.html/other.html keep their static tag as-is.

1. page-type detection + merge (the new core piece)
   - on DOMContentLoad, check for #content-mount in the current document
   - if present (index.html, other.html): shell's already there, go
     straight to mounting
   - if absent (research.html and future content-only pages):
     a. save the page's own body content
     b. fetch('other.html'), parse the response
     c. replace the live body's contents with the fetched shell's body
     d. drop the saved content into the now-present #content-mount
     e. continue into the same mounting step as any other page
   - give content-only pages a real minimal <head> (doctype/meta/
     title/link stylesheet/script src) instead of loose <script> tags
     in the body -- scripts inserted via .innerHTML never execute, so
     as currently written those tags would just go dead once merged
   - add a flash-of-unstyled-content guard (e.g. hide <html> via css
     until js marks it ready) since content-only pages briefly show
     raw unstyled html before the merge finishes

2. MOUNTING (script.js)
   - toolbar buttons into every .toolbar-mount (tool-btn +
     theme-btn/music-btn/video-btn/dice-btn), mounting only the first
     two when the mount also has class="half-toolbar"
   - nav list into #nav-mount (readme/aboutme/research/creative/
     affiliations)
   - platform-link buttons into every .links-mount (substack/spotify/
     letterboxd/goodreads/github/resume/instagram), duplicated when
     the mount is also .marquee
   - write this as a function that runs after step 1's merge (if any)
     so it always sees the real mount points

3. TOOLBAR behavior (script.js)
   - theme-btn: dark/light toggle, rotate 90deg clockwise w/
     transition, starts light
   - music-btn: play/pause bg-audio, mirror-flip (scaleY(-1)) the
     button every 0.5s with no transition while playing, starts
     paused/static
   - video-btn: play/pause bg-video, swap eye.svg / eye-closed.svg,
     starts on eye.svg/paused
   - dice-btn: randomize #photos's image from HEADSHOTS, never
     repeating the current one

4. MARQUEE engine (script.js + style.css)
   - css keyframes (or js-driven) scroll for .marquee-ltr / .marquee-rtl
   - pause on hover, resume on mouse-leave
   - depends on step 2's mounting duplicating content for seamless
     looping

5. research.html's accordion
   - replace the ${accordionSection(...)} calls (dead text as written)
     with a small inline <script> in research.html that calls the
     real accordionSection() from script.js for each section and
     injects the result -- keeps the accordion's content in
     research.html, reuses the one shared builder

6. about-me.html / creative.html / affiliations.html
   - once steps 1-5 are solid for research.html, build the other
     three content-only pages the same way

STYLE (style.css)
- .marquee / .marquee-ltr / .marquee-rtl -- nothing exists yet
- .tool-btn / .theme-btn / .music-btn / .video-btn / .dice-btn -- no
  sizing, no icon coloring
- .link-btn -- no styling at all; turquoise/magenta/blue/etc. vars are
  defined but unused, decide if per-button color cycling is still
  wanted
- .accordion / .accordion-section / .accordion-header /
  .accordion-chevron / .accordion-icon / .accordion-body -- none of
  this exists yet
- dark mode palette -- only one set of (light) variables exists
- #photos img -- no sizing/aspect-ratio/rounding/shadow rules
- #cli -- has spacing but no visual box treatment (no border-radius/
  shadow/background, so it doesn't read as a distinct widget yet)
- .layout still has the "put good margins here" placeholder comment
- #small-toolbar buttons are 10px / #big-toolbar buttons are 30px --
  revisit sizing once real icon content is in them

CONTENT (whenever -- no rush per your answer)
- fill in the empty <a href=""> placeholders in index.html's bio text
- wire the email mention to emailme() or leave as obfuscated text on
  purpose -- currently neither linked nor called anywhere
- lorem ipsum sections in research.html (humans / other animals /
  aliens / ancient people) still need real copy
